# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Finance — environment template
#
# Copy to .env for local development:   cp .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored and is NEVER committed or deployed.
#
# IMPORTANT — these values are read at BUILD time, not at run time.
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the JavaScript bundle when the app is
# built. Putting a .env on the cPanel server has NO effect on an already-built
# app: the bundle is plain static JS and never reads a file from disk. To
# change an endpoint you must rebuild and redeploy.
# (server-php is different — that backend does read its own .env at runtime.)
#
# Never put a secret here — anything VITE_* is public once built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- API endpoint ----------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the server-php API backend for production.
#
# This name is mirrored as a GitHub Actions repository variable
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > Variables). The deploy
# workflow reads it to build for production.
#
# server-php is deployed inside this app's own document root at /api (see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md), so the API is same-origin. Leave this unset and the
# build falls back to "/api", which is what production wants: no CORS grant
# to maintain, and the shared .aicountly.org SSO cookie travels as a
# first-party cookie. Only set it when the API lives on another host.
# PROD_API_BASE_URL=https://finance.aicountly.org/api

# --- Active build config ---------------------------------------------------
# The endpoint this particular build uses. Locally, point it at whichever
# backend you are developing against — the SPA dev server and server-php run
# on different ports, so it must be absolute here. In CI the deploy workflow
# sets it automatically, defaulting to the same-origin /api.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api

# Display name shown in the UI.
VITE_APP_NAME=Finance

# Deploy target this build is for: local | production
VITE_APP_ENV=local

# --- Console SSO ------------------------------------------------------------
# Finance has no login form of its own — console.aicountly.org is the sole
# identity provider (see AUTH_INTEGRATION.md in console-react-app). These
# already default to the real production Console, so they only need to be
# set locally when pointing at a Console dev instance.
# VITE_CONSOLE_URL=https://console.aicountly.org
# VITE_CONSOLE_API_URL=https://console.aicountly.org/api

# --- Subscription invoicing -------------------------------------------------
# No VITE_ variables: the invoicing screens use the same API base URL. Its
# server-side settings (Manage AIC-S2S secrets, GOTENBERG_URL) are in
# server-php/.env.example — never put them here.
